# Fine-grained GitHub personal access token, scoped to ONLY
# chrisjohnson/local-ai-machine-test. Used by scripts/reset_agentic_test_repo.sh
# and by the opencode/Pi agent CLIs (M-021's git-pr-ci-v1 benchmark task) to
# authenticate against that one repo -- deliberately separate from
# secrets/chris_github_key, which is Chris's own SSH key and is scoped to the
# main local-ai-machine repo's deploy-key use only.
#
# How to create it (fine-grained PATs can't be created via `gh`/API, only the
# web UI):
#   1. https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
#   2. Token name: e.g. "local-ai-machine-test-agentic-benchmark"
#   3. Resource owner: chrisjohnson
#   4. Repository access: "Only select repositories" -> local-ai-machine-test
#   5. Permissions (Repository permissions):
#        - Contents: Read and write
#        - Pull requests: Read and write
#        - Actions: Read and write   (needed to watch/re-run CI, list workflow
#          runs; grading also lists runs)
#        - Metadata: Read-only (auto-required, no action needed)
#   6. Generate, copy the token (starts with github_pat_), paste below.
#
# Usage (source before calling gh/git, or before invoking the benchmark
# harness/agent CLIs):
#   set -a; source secrets/gh-agentic-test-repo-token.env; set +a
#   gh auth status   # should show it's using GH_TOKEN, scoped to this one repo
#
# `gh` and most GitHub-aware tooling (opencode, Pi agent's git integration)
# respect GH_TOKEN/GITHUB_TOKEN env vars for authentication automatically.
GH_TOKEN=github_pat_CHANGE_ME
